) VALUES (
  'ga-mphahlele-hosts-provincial-heritage-day-2026-09-28',
  'Ga-Mphahlele hosted Limpopo''s official Heritage Day celebration',
  'Community', '2026-09-28', 'Limpopo Provincial Government', 'https://www.limpopo.gov.za/?p=9578',
  'Limpopo marked Heritage Day on 24 September 2026 with a provincial event at the Sham Rock sports ground in Seleteng, Ga-Mphahlele, in Lepelle-Nkumpi.',
  'The province held its main Heritage Day event on Thursday 24 September 2026 at the Sham Rock sports ground in Seleteng village, Ga-Mphahlele, which falls under Lepelle-Nkumpi Local Municipality in the Capricorn District. According to the Limpopo Provincial Government, Premier Dr Phophi Ramathuba addressed the gathering.

This year the day was marked under the theme of celebrating living heritage and strengthening the ties that bind communities. In her address, the Premier linked heritage to the fight against gender-based violence and femicide, saying, as reported by the provincial government, that traditional and cultural institutions should help teach boys and young men that real strength means respect, responsibility and protecting others.

Capricorn District Municipality says it was chosen to host the provincial celebration this year. Its Executive Mayor, Cllr Mamedupi Teffo, thanked the Premier, traditional leaders, performers, organisers and residents who helped make the day work, and urged communities to keep their languages, music, food and customs alive well beyond Heritage Month.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.limpopo.gov.za/?p=9578", "https://www.cdm.org.za/capricorn-district-extends-appreciation-on-provincial-heritage-day/"]',
  'agent'
);

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news (
  slug, title, category, published_date, source_name, source_url,
  summary, body, image_url, image_credit, image_source, verification_json, source
) VALUES (
  'leeto-f5-route-links-cbd-and-meropa-2026-09-25',
  'Leeto la Polokwane''s new F5 bus route now links the CBD with Meropa',
  'Traffic', '2026-09-25', 'Leeto la Polokwane', 'https://leetolapolokwane.gov.za/2026/09/25/polokwane-marks-new-chapter-in-public-transport-with-launch-of-leeto-f5-meropa-route/',
  'Leeto la Polokwane has added an F5 route between the city centre and Meropa, with a new stop at Meropa Casino and Entertainment World, launched on 6 September.',
  'Commuters who work at or visit Meropa now have a municipal bus option. Leeto la Polokwane, the city''s public transport system, says its new F5 route runs between the Polokwane CBD and Meropa, giving residents, staff and visitors another way to reach the area without a private car or taxi.

The route was officially opened on 6 September 2026. Launch guests boarded a Leeto bus at the Thabo Mbeki Bus Station in town and rode the new route before a ribbon was cut, according to Leeto. Limpopo Premier Dr Phophi Ramathuba and Polokwane Executive Mayor Cllr Makoro John Mpe took part, along with provincial MECs and municipal transport officials.

Limpopo Chronicle reports that the expansion includes a new Leeto stop at Meropa Casino and Entertainment World, launched together with the casino''s management. The mayor described the stop as a step towards better access and connectivity in the city, while the casino said it would make travel easier for its guests and employees.

Passengers planning a trip on the F5 can check routes and journey information on the Leeto la Polokwane website before travelling.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://leetolapolokwane.gov.za/2026/09/25/polokwane-marks-new-chapter-in-public-transport-with-launch-of-leeto-f5-meropa-route/", "https://www.limpopochronicle.co.za/2026/09/07/leeto-la-polokwane-adds-new-bus-stop-at-meropa-casino"]',
  'agent'
);
